From f9d10967f7be57cdbd4066f40ac1dd9d821b14bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiasClear <noreply@biasclear.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:29:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] Explain: wire composed explanations into the handler
 (304 integration)

Port of the 304 integration note onto 19eebb3:
- app.ts and eval/dry-run.ts pass the engine-verified rule id to buildPrompt.
- app.ts refuses, before DynamoDB or a model call, a mark the composer
  can't quote exactly (E_OUT_PLAIN_TEXT) or that no reviewed choice fits
  (E_OUT_HOW): the same answer the checker gives after a call, unpaid.
- Tests and the dry-run stub send reviewed phrase ids. Answers that
  obeyed the text are refused both as free text (E_OUT_SHAPE) and as
  words sent in place of an id (E_OUT_HOW); malformed-output cases use
  the new reply shape.
- New regression: an unquotable engine mark ("Everyone  knows") is
  refused with no table or model call. A mutation that skips the
  pre-check fails it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
